Requirements:
1. world: title is the story's name; setting describes the world (era, place, society, supernatural rules); tone is the tone; rules are world rules that must be followed; style is the narrative style.
2. protagonist: name must be "{{ protagonist_name }}"; summary describes the protagonist's identity and situation without deciding their personality for the player; goal is the protagonist's goal at the opening.
3. characters: the story's key characters, and "{{ card_name }}" must be one of them. For each, write summary (looks, personality, motives), attitude (attitude toward the protagonist) and speech_style (how they speak, learned from the example dialogue). Don't put the protagonist in characters.
4. locations, items, organizations: only what is really needed around the opening; fewer is better. For an item, holder is the name of the character holding it, or location is the name of the place where it is.
5. facts: important facts about the setting, one sentence each; set secret to true for the ones the protagonist doesn't know at first, and list the characters who know them in known_by.
6. opening: location is the opening location (must be a name in locations); present lists the characters present (not the protagonist); situation describes the opening situation; hook is the first hook that sets the story moving.
7. Use names directly; don't leave placeholders such as {{ "{{" }}user{{ "}}" }} or {{ "{{" }}char{{ "}}" }}.
